```

The finding is about SSH (port 22) being open to `0.0.0.0/0`. The fix converts the static `ingress` block into the repo's `dynamic "ingress"` + local-map convention, and restricts the SSH rule's `cidr_blocks` to a trusted, non-internet-wide range (here a placeholder `10.0.0.0/16` -- replace with your actual admin/VPN/bastion CIDR) instead of `0.0.0.0/0`. If broad SSH access is genuinely required, use AWS Systems Manager Session Manager or a bastion/VPN instead of opening port 22 to the internet.
